 "business_summary": "NIKE, Inc. designs, develops, markets and sells athletic footwear, apparel, equipment, accessories and services under the NIKE, Jordan and Converse brands. It describes itself as the largest seller of athletic footwear and apparel in the world. It sells through NIKE Direct (owned stores and digital) and wholesale. Nearly all products are made by contract manufacturers, with Vietnam, Indonesia and China making about 52%, 27% and 16% of NIKE Brand footwear. FY2026 (year ended May 31, 2026) revenue was $46.4B, flat reported and down 2% currency-neutral. Net income was $3.1B, down 3%. Management is mid-way through a product, marketplace and brand reset: it is cutting supply of certain footwear, repositioning digital as full-price, reinvesting in wholesale, and liquidating inventory through markdowns. Greater China and Converse are still declining sharply (Q1 FY27 Greater China -26% currency-neutral, Converse -28%). In October 2026 NIKE announced the multi-year 'Pace' cost program (about $1.0B of pre-tax charges, about $2.5B of cumulative savings through FY2031).",
