 "why_questionable": "Receivables up 26% on flat revenue and supplier finance of $1.1B (about 31% of payables) cut both ways. Receivable growth may reflect weaker collection or more wholesale credit risk, not timing. Supplier finance already props up payables and could reverse. Tax outflows (transition tax, IRS resolution) were disclosed, but more are likely given the uncertain tax positions. Capex also rose from $430M to $684M, and FY25's low capex flatters that year's base."
 },
 {
