 "why_questionable": "The 'shares' field (1.202B) is Class B only. The correct total is about 1.485B. The filings analysis flags this, but the valuation output does not state which count was used. A $51.16 value implies about $76B of equity at 1.485B shares versus about $61.5B at 1.202B shares. If the 1.202B figure leaked into the model, the per-share upside is overstated by about 24%."
 }
 ],
 "inconsistencies_found": [
